assistant: Subject: accept epoch-millisecond created_at in get_order

Vendor version 2026-10-01 now sends `created_at` as a number of milliseconds since 1970 instead of an ISO-8601 string. `get_order` was turning that number into a string and parsing it as a date. That parse failed, the code fell back to `|| 0`, and orders were reported as created on 1970-01-01 with no error. The fix in `src/tools/get_order.ts` uses a numeric `created_at` directly as milliseconds and only parses strings, so old v1 responses still go through the same path and give the same output. I also widened the `VendorOrder.created_at` type to allow both forms. `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm lint` and `pnpm test` all pass, including the repro test and the v1 fixtures.

